        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is huge and resembles a small hill. It lies belly side up in the riverbed. Its belly is exquisite snow-white and covered with a layer of luster. Its back is clear sky blue with a glossy shine, and it has no warts like those on common frogs and toads. Its skin is slippery.",
        "chapters": [
          119
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "From afar it looks hill-like; a person standing at the river edge looks like a tiny monkey beside a large elephant next to it.",
        "chapters": [
          120
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It is a rank five Gu with enormous might that can spit out a river.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It lives in rivers and seas; wave force alone does not wake it while it sleeps.",
        "chapters": [
          120
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "When hungry it opens its mouth and sucks river water in.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It is said that every River Swallowing Toad’s stomach carries a river. The belly need not expand, and the intake can drop a river toward a shallow bed.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Seafood drawn in with the water is not its food, so the toad vomits fish, prawns, turtles, and the like after drinking.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Qing Mao and Jiang Fan beats show only that river-water meal and incidental seafood. No cited chapter shows an owner using the stomach to store non-water goods.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_jiang_fan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "If angered or cornered it can release torrential river water and flood land into marsh. Its natural temper is mild: it loves sleep, has little interest in fighting, and prefers to flee; only when it cannot escape does it counterattack hard.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Other Gu auras put it on alert, and serious injury can drive it to spit a river.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "To send a sleeping toad away without a rampage, Gu Yue elders follow a rumor: one person must wake it by personal strength so it recognizes a local “beast king” and leaves. Using another Gu’s aura, or many people together, fails that recognition and can provoke it.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_yue_clan"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": true,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Tavern talk and Fang Yuan’s own knowledge both treat water as its food.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "feeding",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The Jiang Fan legend adds that it vomits the seafood it does not consume.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "feeding",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "refinement": {
    "recipes": [],
    "used_in_recipes": [],
    "refinement_materials": [],
    "confirmed_evolutions": [],
    "related_variants": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On Black Hair Continent, Fang Yuan’s fake will forces step-by-step guidance until Fang Zheng refines the rank five River Swallowing Toad overnight, naming it as a way to counter the enemy’s water path methods in the next day’s competition.",
        "chapters": [
          1065
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-zhengs-refinement-and-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_black_hair_continent"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Commanding it in battle costs enormous mental energy; when Fang Zheng’s soul is injured, that will tells him he can no longer use the toad as his trump card.",
        "chapters": [
          1084
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-zhengs-refinement-and-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Later, during the hair-continent war inside Lang Ya blessed land, Fang Zheng enters the battlefield standing on the River Swallowing Toad’s back with a rush of tides, and enemies name him the toad Gu Master.",
        "chapters": [
          1167
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-zhengs-refinement-and-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
