  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, clan elders name a rank five River Swallowing Toad that has drifted along the Huang Long River (Yellow Dragon River) to the mountain foot, blocked a river channel, and gone to sleep there.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan later wakes it with tide force and bodily strength and drives it downstream; he does not take the Gu as his own.",
        "chapters": [
          120
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Gu Yue Bo first raises the toad in the elder hall as a three-day-old threat at the mountain foot, warning that a flood could wreck the spirit spring and force an early wolf tide.",
        "chapters": [
          117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-crisis",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_bo"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Chi Shan’s group fails to wake it;",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-crisis",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_chi_shan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan is ordered to try, finds the hill-sized sleeper blocking the channel,",
        "chapters": [
          119
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-crisis",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "and uses incoming tides plus his raised strength to push it about three hundred meters until it wakes. It drinks the river, vomits seafood, exposes Hundred year bitter shells in the drained bed, then swims downstream after looking at Fang Yuan once. The clan promotes him to team leader and awards five hundred primeval stones for chasing it away.",
        "chapters": [
          120
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-crisis",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan never used a River Swallowing Toad in his previous life, but remembers Jiang Fan, a mortal fishery servant whose story spreads about two hundred years later in that timeline. A sleeping toad blocks Jiang Fan’s water; after days of complaint and kinship, it wakes, drinks the river, and vomits a mountain of seafood that saves his quota. When Gu Masters try to expel the rank five Gu, it carries Jiang Fan and floods the village; thereafter people treat him as owning a rank five Gu worm even though he has no awakened aperture. He founds a hamlet, is assassinated, and the toad leaves after his death.",
        "chapters": [
          118
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-host-legend",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters",
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later teaching also cites the Jiang Fan case as a human example of borrowing a Gu worm’s ability without being a Gu Master.",
        "chapters": [
          157
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-host-legend",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
